  ('N10.2-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A no-pets apartment building receives a request from a tenant with a disability to keep an assistance animal. Generally, the landlord must:', '["Refuse because of the no-pets rule","Make a reasonable accommodation and allow it","Charge a pet deposit","Require the tenant to move to a pet-friendly building"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Reasonable accommodations in rules, like allowing an assistance animal, are required for people with disabilities.', '["Fair housing law requires reasonable accommodations in rules.","","Assistance animals aren''t pets; pet fees generally can''t be charged.","That isn''t an accommodation."]'::jsonb, 'Modify the place. Accommodate the rules.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'assistance-animal-accommodation', 'unverified'),
