  ('N10.3-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'A past client clicks "unsubscribe" on your monthly market email. You should:', '["Move them to your text message list instead","Stop sending them marketing email promptly, within the time CAN-SPAM allows","Send one more email asking why","Keep sending because they''re a past client"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Opt-out requests must be honored promptly; CAN-SPAM allows up to 10 business days.', '["Texting without consent can violate the TCPA.","","Further marketing email after opt-out isn''t allowed.","Being a past client doesn''t override an opt-out."]'::jsonb, 'Let them opt out, and mean it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'unsubscribe-honor', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.3-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'A team may advertise using only its team name, without showing its brokerage.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False.', '["Team ads generally must identify the brokerage, as state rules set out.",""]'::jsonb, 'Name the brokerage. Tell the truth.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'team-name-brokerage-required', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.3-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'The core rule for real estate advertising is that it must be:', '["Truthful and not misleading","Approved by the MLS","Printed in a newspaper","Free of any opinions"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Advertising must be accurate and not misleading.', '["","MLS approval isn''t required.","No particular medium is required.","Puffing opinions are allowed; false facts aren''t."]'::jsonb, 'Advertise what''s real.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'advertising-truthful', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.3-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'An agent wants to send listing flyers by fax to businesses that never asked for them. Generally:', '["Unsolicited advertising faxes are restricted by federal law","It''s allowed for commercial property only","It''s always allowed","It''s allowed after 9 p.m."]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'The TCPA, as amended, restricts unsolicited advertising faxes.', '["","There''s no general commercial exception.","Federal law restricts unsolicited ad faxes.","Time of day doesn''t change the rule."]'::jsonb, 'No consent, no fax.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'fax-unsolicited', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Real estate commission rates are:', '["Set by the local board","Set by the MLS","Set by state law","Negotiable between each broker and client"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Commissions are always negotiable.', '["Boards can''t set rates; that would be price fixing.","The MLS can''t set rates.","No law sets commission rates.",""]'::jsonb, 'Every commission is negotiable.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'commissions-negotiable', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'Brokers from competing firms agree at a meeting that none of them will list for less than 6%. This is:', '["A tie-in","Price fixing","Market allocation","A group boycott"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Competitors agreeing on rates is price fixing, a Sherman Act violation.', '["A tie-in conditions one service on another.","","Market allocation divides territories or customers.","A boycott refuses to deal with someone."]'::jsonb, 'Never talk rates with the competition.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'price-fixing-discussion', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'Several brokers agree not to show listings of a new discount brokerage. This is:', '["A group boycott","Puffing","Steering","Price fixing"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Competitors agreeing to shut out a firm is a group boycott.', '["","Puffing is opinion in ads.","Steering is a fair housing violation.","No prices were agreed."]'::jsonb, 'Don''t fix, boycott, divide, or tie.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'group-boycott-example', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'Two brokerages agree that one will handle homes over $1 million and the other homes under $1 million. This is:', '["A legal business plan","Market allocation","A tie-in","Price fixing"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Dividing customers or price ranges among competitors is market allocation.', '["Agreements between competitors to divide markets are illegal.","","No purchase is tied to another.","No rates were agreed."]'::jsonb, 'Don''t fix, boycott, divide, or tie.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'market-allocation-example', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A developer-broker will sell a lot only to buyers who agree to list their current home with the broker. This is:', '["An option","Market allocation","A boycott","A tie-in arrangement"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Conditioning one sale on buying another service is a tie-in.', '["An option is a right to buy.","Nothing is divided among competitors.","No one is being shut out by competitors.",""]'::jsonb, 'Don''t fix, boycott, divide, or tie.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'tie-in-example', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Under the Sherman Act, an individual convicted of a criminal antitrust violation can face:', '["A warning letter only","A $500 fine","Fines up to $1 million and up to 10 years in prison","License suspension only"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Individuals face up to $1 million in fines and 10 years in prison; corporations up to $100 million.', '["Antitrust violations are serious crimes.","Penalties are much larger.","","Criminal penalties go beyond licensing."]'::jsonb, 'Antitrust: million-dollar mistakes.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'sherman-penalties-individual', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'At a networking lunch, competing agents start agreeing on what "everyone should charge." What should the agent do?', '["Agree, since it helps the industry","Share your own rate floor","Stay quiet and nod along","Object, leave the conversation, and make it clear you set your fees independently"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Even appearing to join a price discussion is risky. Leave and make your independence clear.', '["Agreeing makes you part of price fixing.","Sharing invites an agreement.","Silence while others agree can look like participation.",""]'::jsonb, 'Never talk rates with the competition.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-overhears-rate-talk', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'A broker may set their own firm''s commission policy independently.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","Setting your own prices independently is legal; agreeing with competitors isn''t."]'::jsonb, 'Your rate is your decision alone.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'broker-own-rate-ok', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Telling a seller, "The standard commission here is 6%," is a safe statement.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. There''s no standard rate; say what your firm charges and that it''s negotiable.', '["Implying a standard rate suggests rates aren''t negotiable and can look like price fixing.",""]'::jsonb, 'Every commission is negotiable.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'standard-rate-statement', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which federal law is the primary source of antitrust rules for real estate brokers?', '["TILA","Fair Housing Act","Sherman Antitrust Act","RESPA"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'The Sherman Act prohibits agreements in restraint of trade.', '["TILA covers credit disclosures.","The FHA covers discrimination.","","RESPA covers settlement procedures."]'::jsonb, 'Sherman stops the scheming.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'antitrust-law-name', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'A seller mentions a discount brokerage. Which response best avoids antitrust problems?', '["\"Their agents are unlicensed.\"","\"We all agreed not to work with them.\"","\"No one in town will show your home if you list there.\"","\"Here''s what our firm offers and charges. You can compare and decide.\""]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Compete on your own value and fees. Never imply collective action against a competitor.', '["A false claim about a competitor is misrepresentation.","That admits a group boycott.","Predicting a boycott can suggest one exists.",""]'::jsonb, 'Compete on value, not collusion.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-statement-competitor-low-fee', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Salespeople at the same brokerage following the broker''s fee policy are not engaged in price fixing.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. Price fixing requires an agreement among competitors.', '["","One firm setting its own policy isn''t an agreement among competitors."]'::jsonb, 'Your rate is your decision alone.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'salespeople-same-firm-rate-policy', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A person harmed by an antitrust violation may sue and recover:', '["Up to three times their actual damages","Nothing; only the government can act","Only an apology","Only their actual damages"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Private antitrust plaintiffs can recover treble damages.', '["","Private suits are allowed.","That''s not a remedy.","Antitrust law allows treble damages."]'::jsonb, 'Triple damages, triple trouble.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'antitrust-civil-damages', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'Two agents from different firms agree, "You take the north side of town, I''ll take the south." This is:', '["A designated agency","Illegal market allocation","A legal referral network","Fair competition"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Competitors dividing territories is market allocation.', '["Designated agency is about representation within one firm.","","Referral networks don''t divide markets.","Dividing territories eliminates competition."]'::jsonb, 'Don''t fix, boycott, divide, or tie.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'allocation-by-territory', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.4-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Price fixing is illegal even if the agreed prices are reasonable.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","Price fixing is illegal per se; reasonableness is no defense."]'::jsonb, 'Never talk rates with the competition.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'antitrust-no-intent-needed-price', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.5-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Which best describes a salesperson working as an independent contractor?', '["Receives employee health benefits","Paid on results, controls their own methods, pays their own taxes","Paid hourly with taxes withheld","Required to work set office hours"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Independent contractors are paid by results and control how they work.', '["Benefits point toward employee status.","","That describes an employee.","Set hours point toward employee status."]'::jsonb, 'Paid by results, not by hours.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'independent-contractor-paid-results', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.5-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'For the IRS to treat a real estate agent as a statutory nonemployee, which is required?', '["Working fewer than 20 hours a week","Being paid only in cash","A license, pay based on sales rather than hours, and a written contract saying they aren''t treated as an employee for taxes","Owning a business entity"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'The IRS test: licensed, paid on output, and a written contract stating non-employee tax treatment.', '["Hours aren''t the test.","Cash payment isn''t a test and isn''t allowed outside the broker anyway.","","No entity is required."]'::jsonb, 'License, results, written contract.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'statutory-nonemployee-tests', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.5-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'Even though salespeople are independent contractors for tax purposes, the broker must still:', '["Set their working hours","Pay their health insurance","Withhold their income taxes","Supervise their real estate activities as license law requires"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Tax status doesn''t change the broker''s duty to supervise under license law.', '["Controlling hours suggests employment.","Benefits aren''t required for contractors.","Contractors pay their own taxes.",""]'::jsonb, 'Contractor for taxes, supervised by law.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'broker-still-supervises-ic', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.5-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A salesperson may receive compensation for real estate work from:', '["The seller directly, if the seller insists","The title company","Any party to the transaction","Only their own broker"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'All compensation flows through the employing broker.', '["Even the seller must pay through the broker.","Title companies don''t pay licensees for brokerage work.","Payments from others must go through the broker.",""]'::jsonb, 'All pay flows through the broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'salesperson-paid-only-by-broker', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.5-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'Your happy buyer offers you a $1,000 cash bonus at closing. What should the agent do?', '["Explain it must be paid through your broker and handled as required, and check office policy","Ask for a check made out to you personally","Accept the cash privately","Ask them to give it to your spouse"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Compensation for real estate work must go through your broker.', '["","Still bypasses the broker.","Payment outside the broker violates license law.","Routing it through others is still improper."]'::jsonb, 'All pay flows through the broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-client-offers-cash-bonus', 'unverified'),
