  ('N10.5-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A broker receives a $15,000 commission on a sale. The salesperson''s agreement gives them 70%. How much does the salesperson receive?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":10500,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '70% of $15,000 is $10,500.', '[]'::jsonb, 'All pay flows through the broker, then splits.', 'Salesperson share = broker''s commission × split %', '["70% = 0.70.","$15,000 × 0.70 = $10,500."]'::jsonb, null, 'salesperson-split-calc', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.5-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'If a brokerage treats a salesperson as an employee, the brokerage generally must:', '["Withhold income and payroll taxes","Avoid supervising them","Pay the salesperson only on closed deals","Pay them through the title company"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Employers withhold taxes for employees.', '["","Supervision is still required.","Employees can be paid other ways; withholding is the key obligation.","Pay always flows through the broker."]'::jsonb, 'Employee: taxes withheld.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'employee-tax-withholding', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.5-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'Why should a brokerage have a written independent contractor agreement with each salesperson?', '["It replaces the salesperson''s license","It ends the broker''s responsibility","It''s part of the IRS test and documents duties, splits, and supervision","It lets salespeople pay themselves directly"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'The written agreement supports tax status and sets expectations.', '["Nothing replaces the license.","The broker stays responsible under license law.","","Pay still flows through the broker."]'::jsonb, 'License, results, written contract.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'ic-agreement-written', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.5-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'You''re unsure whether a contract addendum is filled out correctly. What should the agent do?', '["Have your client fill it in","Send it and hope for the best","Ask your broker or designated supervisor before it goes out","Ask the other agent to fix it"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Use your broker''s supervision. That''s what it''s for.', '["Shifting your job to the client isn''t appropriate.","Guessing on contracts creates risk for your client.","","The other agent represents the other side."]'::jsonb, 'When in doubt, ask your broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-ask-broker-unsure', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.5-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'A salesperson may operate a brokerage independently without being supervised by a broker.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False.', '["Salespeople must work under a licensed broker.",""]'::jsonb, 'Salesperson works through the broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'salesperson-own-brokerage-no', 'unverified'),
