  ('N10.5-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A salesperson leaves a brokerage while a deal they worked on is still pending. Any commission they''re owed on it is generally paid:', '["By the new broker","By the client directly","By the former broker, according to their agreement","Never"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'The original broker earned the commission and pays the salesperson under their agreement.', '["The new broker wasn''t involved.","Clients don''t pay salespeople directly.","","Earned pay may still be owed under the agreement."]'::jsonb, 'All pay flows through the broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'salesperson-change-broker-pay', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Errors and omissions insurance generally covers:', '["Intentional fraud","Negligent mistakes in professional work","Criminal fines","The licensee''s car accidents"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'E&O covers honest professional mistakes, not fraud.', '["E&O doesn''t cover intentional wrongdoing.","","Fines for crimes aren''t covered.","That''s auto insurance."]'::jsonb, 'E&O covers errors, not lies.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'eo-insurance-covers', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 1, 'application', 'A buyer receives an email that appears to be from the title company with "updated wiring instructions." The buyer should:', '["Call the number in the email","Reply to the email to confirm","Call the title company at a known, independently verified number before wiring","Wire immediately to avoid delaying closing"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Always verify wiring instructions by calling a known number, never one in the email.', '["The number in a fake email reaches the scammer.","Replying goes straight to the scammer.","","Speed is what scammers count on."]'::jsonb, 'Never trust a wire email. Call a known number.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'wire-fraud-verify-phone', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'When should you warn clients about wire fraud?', '["Never, it''s the title company''s job","Only after money goes missing","Only if they ask","At the start of the transaction, and again before closing"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Early and repeated warnings are the best defense.', '["Everyone in the transaction has a role in prevention.","By then the money may be gone.","Many don''t know to ask.",""]'::jsonb, 'Warn early, warn again.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-warn-wire-fraud-early', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which is a sound risk-management practice?', '["Documenting important conversations and decisions in writing","Skipping disclosures to keep deals simple","Giving legal advice to save clients money","Using homemade contract forms"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Written records protect clients and the licensee.', '["","Skipped disclosures create liability.","Legal advice is outside a licensee''s role.","Approved, tested forms reduce risk."]'::jsonb, 'Write it down, and refer what you don''t know.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'risk-management-practices', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which is true about a professional association''s Code of Ethics?', '["It binds every licensee in the state","It''s the same as state license law","It binds the association''s members and can be stricter than license law","It''s enforced by the Real Estate Division"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Codes of Ethics are association rules for members; license law comes from the state.', '["It applies only to members.","License law is enacted by the state.","","The association enforces its own code."]'::jsonb, 'Law is the floor. Ethics can raise the bar.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'code-ethics-vs-license-law', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Brokers must keep transaction records for the period state law requires.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. Nevada''s period is covered in the state units.', '["","Record retention periods are set by state law."]'::jsonb, 'Keep it as long as the law says.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'records-retain-required', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'E&O insurance will protect a licensee who knowingly hides a defect.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False.', '["Intentional misconduct is excluded from E&O coverage.",""]'::jsonb, 'E&O covers errors, not lies.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'eo-covers-fraud-false', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'Which is the safest way to handle clients'' sensitive documents, like bank statements?', '["Use your brokerage''s secure document system and limit who can access them","Keep them in a public cloud folder anyone can open","Text them to your personal phone","Print copies for every party"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Protect client data with secure, limited-access systems.', '["","Open folders expose private data.","Personal devices without controls raise exposure.","Printing extras multiplies the risk."]'::jsonb, 'Private data, private place.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'cybersecurity-client-docs', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'scenario', 3, 'application', 'You discover your email account was hacked during an active transaction. What should the agent do?', '["Change the password and say nothing","Delete the account","Wait to see if anything happens","Tell your broker, the title or escrow company, and your clients immediately, and warn them not to trust any emailed wiring instructions"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'A compromised email is a wire-fraud emergency. Alert everyone right away.', '["Silence leaves clients exposed to fraud.","Deleting the account doesn''t warn anyone and may destroy records.","Waiting can cost clients their closing funds.",""]'::jsonb, 'Hacked? Warn everyone, now.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-email-hacked', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Why do brokerages use standard, approved contract forms?', '["To raise commissions","To avoid disclosures","Because handwritten contracts are illegal","To reduce errors and avoid licensees drafting legal language"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Approved forms keep licensees from practicing law and reduce mistakes.', '["Forms don''t set commissions.","Forms often include disclosures.","Handwritten terms can be valid; the issue is legal drafting by non-lawyers.",""]'::jsonb, 'Fill in forms; don''t write law.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'standard-forms-reduce-risk', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A client asks whether a 1031 exchange makes sense for them. The best response is:', '["Explain it''s a tax question and recommend a CPA or tax attorney","Say no, they''re too complicated","Prepare the exchange paperwork yourself","Say yes, it always saves taxes"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Tax advice belongs with tax professionals.', '["","That''s also tax advice.","Exchanges involve specialized tax and legal work.","That''s tax advice, and not always true."]'::jsonb, 'Know your lane. Refer the rest.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'outside-expertise-refer', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'State license law sets the legal minimum standards for licensee conduct.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","License law is the floor everyone must meet."]'::jsonb, 'Law is the floor.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'license-law-is-minimum', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which is a common sign of a wire-fraud email?', '["A message during business hours","Urgent request to wire to a new account, from an address that''s slightly off","A greeting with the client''s name","An attached disclosure form"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Last-minute account changes and look-alike addresses are classic red flags.', '["Timing alone isn''t a sign.","","Scammers often know names from hacked accounts.","Attachments alone aren''t a sign."]'::jsonb, 'New account + urgency = stop and call.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'fake-email-signs', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'An agent notices a typo in the purchase price that favors their client by $10,000. The ethical step is:', '["Wait until after closing","Say nothing because it benefits the client","Point out the error so the documents reflect the actual agreement","Tell only the client"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Honesty and fair dealing mean correcting known errors.', '["Waiting makes the problem worse.","Taking advantage of a known mistake isn''t honest dealing.","","The documents must reflect the real agreement for everyone."]'::jsonb, 'Honest with everyone.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'fairness-all-parties-ethics', 'unverified'),
  ('N10.6-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N10', 'N10.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'LAW', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Relying on verbal agreements for repairs reduces risk because there''s less paperwork to get wrong.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False.', '["Verbal agreements are hard to prove. Put agreements in writing.",""]'::jsonb, 'Write it down.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'verbal-agreements-risk', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'In an agency relationship, the person who hires the agent and is owed fiduciary duties is the:', '["Customer","Principal","Third party","Subagent"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'The principal, or client, hires the agent and is owed fiduciary duties.', '["A customer is not represented.","","Third parties are outside the agency.","A subagent is an agent of the agent."]'::jsonb, 'Clients get loyalty. Customers get honesty.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'principal-is-client', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A broker hired to find a buyer for one property is usually what type of agent?', '["Special agent","Subagent","Universal agent","General agent"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'A broker hired for one task is a special agent.', '["","A subagent works under another agent.","Universal agents can do anything the principal can.","General agents handle a range of matters in a business."]'::jsonb, 'Special: one task.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'listing-broker-special-agent', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A property manager who collects rents, signs leases, and hires repair vendors for an owner is typically a:', '["Special agent","Universal agent","General agent","Customer"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Authority to handle a range of matters within one business makes a general agent.', '["The manager handles a range of tasks, not just one.","The authority is limited to managing this business, not everything.","","The manager represents the owner."]'::jsonb, 'General: a business.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'property-manager-general-agent', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Someone holding a broad general power of attorney to handle all of another person''s affairs is a:', '["Subagent","Universal agent","Special agent","General agent"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Authority to do anything the principal could lawfully do makes a universal agent.', '["A subagent works for another agent.","","Special agents have one task.","General agents are limited to one business."]'::jsonb, 'Universal: all.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'universal-agent-poa', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A listing agent shows the home to an unrepresented buyer. The buyer is the agent''s:', '["Client, owed fiduciary duties","Principal","Customer, owed honesty and fair dealing","Subagent"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Unrepresented parties are customers. They''re owed honesty, not loyalty.', '["The agent represents the seller, not the buyer.","The seller is the principal.","","A buyer isn''t an agent."]'::jsonb, 'Clients get loyalty. Customers get honesty.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'customer-owed-honesty', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A cooperating broker who agrees to work on behalf of the listing broker to sell the seller''s home is a:', '["Universal agent","Buyer''s agent","Transaction broker","Subagent of the seller"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'An agent working through the listing broker for the seller is a subagent.', '["Nothing gives universal authority.","This broker works for the seller''s side, not the buyer.","A transaction broker represents no one.",""]'::jsonb, 'Subagent: an agent of the agent.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'subagent-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'One licensee represents both the buyer and the seller in the same transaction. This is:', '["Subagency","Special agency","Single agency","Dual agency"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Representing both parties in one deal is dual agency, which requires informed consent where permitted.', '["Subagency is acting through another agent.","Special agency describes scope, not sides.","Single agency means one side only.",""]'::jsonb, 'Two clients, one firm: disclose and get consent.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'dual-agency-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A broker assigns one licensee to represent the seller and a different licensee in the same firm to represent the buyer. This is called:', '["Designated or assigned agency","Undisclosed dual agency","Subagency","Universal agency"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Assigning separate licensees within one firm to each party is designated agency. Nevada calls it assigned agency.', '["","This arrangement is disclosed and structured.","Subagency doesn''t involve separate representation.","The scope isn''t universal."]'::jsonb, 'Same firm, different agents, each side covered.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'designated-agency-two-licensees', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'In states that allow it, a transaction broker:', '["Helps both parties complete the deal without representing either","Can''t be paid","Represents both parties with full loyalty","Represents only the seller"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'A transaction broker facilitates without an agency relationship, as allowed by state law.', '["","Transaction brokers can be paid.","Full loyalty to both isn''t possible; that''s why it''s non-agency.","That''s single agency."]'::jsonb, 'Facilitator: helps the deal, represents no one.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'transaction-broker-no-rep', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'At your listing''s open house, an unrepresented buyer asks, "What''s the lowest the seller will take?" What should the agent do?', '["Ask the buyer to sign a buyer agreement so you can tell them","Explain that you represent the seller and can''t share the seller''s bottom line, and offer to present any offer","Guess a number","Share the seller''s lowest acceptable price to keep the buyer interested"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'The seller is your client. Keep their confidential information private and treat the buyer honestly.', '["Signing up the buyer doesn''t release you from duties to the seller.","","Guessing may still mislead or reveal confidential information.","That breaches confidentiality to your client."]'::jsonb, 'Clients get loyalty. Customers get honesty.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-unrepresented-buyer-advice', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'A salesperson acts as an agent of their broker, and through the broker for the client.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. The broker is the client''s agent; the salesperson acts for the broker.', '["","Salespeople work under and on behalf of their broker."]'::jsonb, 'Salesperson works through the broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'salesperson-agent-of-broker', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'A dual agent can give full, undivided loyalty to both buyer and seller.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. Dual agency limits loyalty, which is why consent is required.', '["Full loyalty to both sides is impossible when their interests conflict. That''s why dual agency requires informed consent and limits duties.",""]'::jsonb, 'Two masters, divided loyalty.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'dual-agent-full-loyalty-both', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Who pays the commission determines whom the broker represents.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. A buyer''s agent can be paid from the seller''s proceeds and still represent the buyer.', '["Agency is created by agreement or conduct, not by who pays.",""]'::jsonb, 'Payment doesn''t decide loyalty.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'payment-not-determine-agency', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'One risk for a seller who allows subagency is that:', '["The listing becomes open","The seller may be liable for a subagent''s misrepresentations","The seller loses the right to approve offers","The seller must pay two full commissions by law"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Because subagents act for the seller, the seller can be liable for their wrongful acts.', '["Subagency doesn''t change the listing type.","","The seller still decides on offers.","Commission terms come from the agreements, not a law requiring two."]'::jsonb, 'More agents, more liability.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'vicarious-liability-subagent', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Representing only the buyer or only the seller in a transaction is:', '["Ostensible agency","Universal agency","Dual agency","Single agency"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Single agency means one client in the transaction.', '["Ostensible agency is created by appearances.","Universal describes scope of authority.","Dual agency represents both.",""]'::jsonb, 'Single: one side.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'single-agency-def', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A buyer working with the listing agent but not represented is a customer. Which must the agent still do for that buyer?', '["Disclose known material defects honestly","Negotiate the lowest price for the buyer","Advise the buyer on how much to offer","Keep the buyer''s top price from the seller"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Customers are owed honesty, including disclosure of known material defects.', '["","Negotiating for the buyer would be acting against the client.","Advising the customer on price is acting as their advocate.","The agent owes confidentiality to the seller, not the buyer."]'::jsonb, 'Honest with everyone. Loyal to your client.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-buyer-customer-duties', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-17', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'In agency language, the person the agent deals with on the principal''s behalf is the:', '["Fiduciary","Principal","Attorney-in-fact","Third party"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'The agent deals with third parties on the principal''s behalf.', '["The agent is the fiduciary.","The principal hired the agent.","An attorney-in-fact is an agent under a power of attorney.",""]'::jsonb, 'Agent in the middle: principal behind, third party across.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agency-third-party', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.1-18', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which statement about agency in real estate is most accurate?', '["Agency exists only when a commission is paid","Only federal law governs agency","Agency rules are the same in every state","Common law sets general duties, and each state''s statutes can add or change the rules"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'General agency principles come from common law, but each state, including Nevada, sets its own statutory rules.', '["Agency can exist without a commission.","Agency is mostly state law.","States differ significantly.",""]'::jsonb, 'Common law sets the floor; states build the house.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agency-law-common-statute', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A signed listing agreement creates what kind of agency?', '["Implied agency","Agency by ratification","Express agency","Ostensible agency"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'An agency created by a stated agreement is express.', '["Implied agency comes from conduct, not a stated agreement.","Ratification approves past acts.","","Ostensible agency comes from appearances."]'::jsonb, 'Agreement, actions, approval after, or appearances.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'express-agency-listing', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A principal approves, after the fact, an act an agent did without authority. This creates agency by:', '["Ratification","Express agreement","Estoppel","Operation of law"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Approving an unauthorized act afterward is ratification.', '["","There was no prior agreement.","Estoppel comes from misleading appearances to a third party.","Operation of law ends agencies; it doesn''t create this one."]'::jsonb, 'Ratify: approve it after.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'ratification-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'An owner lets a third party reasonably believe a person is the owner''s agent, and the third party relies on it. The owner may be bound by:', '["A net listing","Ostensible agency (agency by estoppel)","Ratification","Novation"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'When a principal creates the appearance of agency, the law can hold them to it.', '["A net listing is a listing type.","","Ratification requires the principal to approve an act afterward.","Novation substitutes a contract."]'::jsonb, 'Appearances can create an agent.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'estoppel-agency', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'Without signing anything, a licensee advises a buyer on what to offer, and the buyer relies on that advice. The licensee may have created:', '["No relationship at all","A universal agency","An implied agency with the buyer","A land contract"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Acting like the buyer''s advocate can create an implied agency, with all its duties.', '["Conduct can create an agency.","Nothing suggests authority over everything.","","A land contract is a sale."]'::jsonb, 'Actions can sign a contract too.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'implied-agency-conduct', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A listing ends when the home sells and the transaction closes. This is termination by:', '["Performance","Operation of law","Revocation","Renunciation"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Completing the agency''s purpose ends it by performance.', '["","Operation of law covers events like death or bankruptcy.","Revocation is the principal withdrawing authority.","Renunciation is the agent giving it up."]'::jsonb, 'Done means done.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agency-ends-performance', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'When the agent, not the principal, ends the agency, it''s called:', '["Revocation","Ratification","Rescission","Renunciation"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'An agent renounces; a principal revokes.', '["Revocation is by the principal.","Ratification creates agency.","Rescission cancels a contract by agreement or right.",""]'::jsonb, 'Principal revokes. Agent renounces.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'renunciation-agent-ends', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which agency can''t be revoked by the principal?', '["An agency coupled with an interest","A buyer agency agreement","An exclusive right to sell","An open listing"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'When the agent holds an interest in the property, the agency is irrevocable.', '["","Buyer agreements can be revoked, possibly with damages.","A principal can revoke an exclusive listing, though they may owe damages.","Open listings can be revoked."]'::jsonb, 'Own a piece, can''t be fired.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'coupled-interest-irrevocable', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Which event ends an agency by operation of law?', '["An open house","A new MLS photo","The principal''s death","A price change"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Death, incapacity, bankruptcy, and destruction of the property end agency by law.', '["Marketing doesn''t end the agency.","Marketing changes don''t matter.","","Changing terms doesn''t end the agency."]'::jsonb, 'If a person goes, the agency goes.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agency-ends-death-principal', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'You''re the listing agent, and an unrepresented buyer starts asking your advice on strategy. What should the agent do to avoid creating an accidental agency?', '["Give advice freely and clarify only if asked","Stop talking to the buyer entirely","Clarify early, as required, that you represent the seller and explain what that means for the buyer","Tell the buyer you represent everyone"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Clear, timely disclosure of whom you represent prevents implied agency and misunderstandings.', '["Advising first can create an implied agency.","You can still provide honest information and show the home.","","That''s misleading."]'::jsonb, 'Say who you work for before they say too much.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-avoid-accidental-agency', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'An agency relationship can exist even if the agent isn''t paid.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. Duties come from the relationship, not the paycheck.', '["","Compensation isn''t required for agency or its duties."]'::jsonb, 'No pay, still a duty.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agency-without-compensation', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'A principal who revokes an agency without cause before the term ends may owe the agent damages.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. Power to revoke isn''t the same as the right to revoke without consequence.', '["","The principal has the power to revoke, but breaching the contract can cost them."]'::jsonb, 'You can fire your agent; you may have to pay for it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'revocation-may-owe-damages', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Once an agency ends, the agent may freely share the former client''s confidential information.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. Confidentiality survives termination.', '["The duty of confidentiality continues after the agency ends.",""]'::jsonb, 'Secrets don''t expire with the listing.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'confidentiality-survives-termination', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'During a listing, the seller files for bankruptcy and a court-appointed trustee takes control of the property. The listing most likely:', '["Converts to an open listing","Continues unchanged","Becomes an agency coupled with an interest","Ends by operation of law; the agent must work with the trustee on any new agreement"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Bankruptcy can terminate the agency by operation of law.', '["Nothing converts it.","The seller no longer controls the property.","The agent gains no ownership interest.",""]'::jsonb, 'If the owner loses control, the listing ends.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'bankruptcy-ends-agency', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A buyer agreement reaches its end date without a purchase. The agency ends by:', '["Expiration","Ratification","Performance","Renunciation"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Reaching the agreed end date terminates the agency.', '["","Ratification creates agency.","Nothing was performed.","Neither party gave notice."]'::jsonb, 'Every agreement needs an end date.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agency-ends-expiration', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A listed home burns down. The listing agency:', '["Continues for the land only, automatically","Becomes an exclusive agency","Continues unless the broker cancels","Ends by operation of law"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Destruction of the property ends the agency by law.', '["The parties could make a new agreement for the land, but it''s not automatic.","Nothing changes it into another type.","It ends without anyone canceling.",""]'::jsonb, 'No property, no listing.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'destruction-ends-agency', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A seller gives a broker authority to market and find a buyer. Without more, the broker can:', '["Sign the deed for the seller","Lower the price without asking","Accept offers for the seller","Present offers but not sign a contract binding the seller"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'A listing broker is a special agent with limited authority: find a buyer, not bind the seller.', '["Signing a deed needs a recorded power of attorney.","Price changes need the seller''s approval.","A listing doesn''t give authority to bind the seller.",""]'::jsonb, 'Special agent, limited authority.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agency-authority-scope', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-17', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'scenario', 3, 'application', 'Your seller emails that they''re firing your brokerage today. What should the agent do?', '["Stop acting as the seller''s agent, tell your broker immediately, and let the broker address any contract issues","Keep showing the home until the listing date expires","Ignore the email until a lawyer calls","Tell buyers the seller is in breach"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'A principal can revoke authority at any time. Stop acting, and let the broker handle the contract consequences.', '["","Once authority is revoked, continuing to act is unauthorized.","Ignoring it risks acting without authority.","Disparaging the client breaches duties and may be false."]'::jsonb, 'Fired means stop, then let the broker sort it out.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-revocation-stop-marketing', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.2-18', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'A principal and agent can end an agency at any time by mutual agreement.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","Both parties can agree to end it."]'::jsonb, 'Agreed to start, agree to stop.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agency-mutual-agreement-ends', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Which list matches the fiduciary duties an agent owes a client?', '["Obedience, licensing, disclosure, commission, advertising, records","Loyalty, lending, disclosure, compliance, appraisal, repairs","Openness, liability, discretion, care, appraisal, results","Obedience, loyalty, disclosure, confidentiality, accounting, reasonable care"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'OLDCAR lists the six fiduciary duties.', '["Licensing, commission and advertising aren''t fiduciary duties.","Lending and appraisal aren''t fiduciary duties.","This list mixes in made-up duties.",""]'::jsonb, 'OLDCAR: the six things a client is owed.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'oldcar-duties-list', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A seller instructs the listing agent not to show the home to buyers of a certain religion. The agent should:', '["Follow it only for showings, not offers","Refuse, because the instruction is illegal","Follow it under the duty of obedience","Ask the broker to follow it instead"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'The duty of obedience covers lawful instructions only. This one violates fair housing law.', '["Discrimination at any stage is illegal.","","Obedience extends only to lawful instructions.","No licensee can lawfully follow it."]'::jsonb, 'Obey the lawful. Refuse the unlawful.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'obedience-lawful-only', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A listing agent learns the buyer would pay $15,000 more than offered. Under the duty of disclosure, the agent should:', '["Tell the buyer''s agent","Tell the seller","Tell no one","Keep it from the seller"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'An agent must tell the client every material fact, including the other side''s willingness to pay more.', '["The buyer''s agent already knows; this doesn''t serve the client.","","The client is entitled to material facts.","Hiding material information from the client breaches disclosure."]'::jsonb, 'Tell your client everything.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'disclosure-buyer-higher-price', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A seller tells the listing agent they''re divorcing and must sell fast. A buyer''s agent asks why they''re selling. The listing agent should:', '["Explain the divorce to show urgency","Tell the buyer''s agent off the record","Keep the seller''s reasons confidential","Say they''ll take any offer"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Confidential information that could hurt the client''s position stays private.', '["Revealing it weakens the client''s negotiating position.","Off the record is still a disclosure.","","That reveals the client''s position."]'::jsonb, 'Tell others nothing private.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'confidentiality-seller-motivation', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'The duty to safeguard and report on all client money and documents is:', '["Loyalty","Obedience","Reasonable care","Accounting"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Accounting covers handling money and property for the client.', '["Loyalty is about putting the client first.","Obedience is following lawful instructions.","Reasonable care is about competence.",""]'::jsonb, 'Accounting: every dollar tracked.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'accounting-duty', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'An agent who has never handled farm property takes a 200-acre ranch listing without help and badly misprices it. Which duty is most at issue?', '["Accounting","Obedience","Confidentiality","Reasonable care and diligence"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Agents must use the skill of a competent licensee, which means getting help or referring work beyond their expertise.', '["No money was mishandled.","No instruction was disobeyed.","No private information was shared.",""]'::jsonb, 'Know your lane. Refer the rest.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'reasonable-care-competence', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Putting the client''s interests above everyone else''s, including the agent''s own commission, is the duty of:', '["Disclosure","Accounting","Loyalty","Obedience"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Loyalty means the client''s interests come first.', '["Disclosure is sharing material facts.","Accounting is about money.","","Obedience is following instructions."]'::jsonb, 'Client first, commission second.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'loyalty-above-own', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'Representing a buyer, you notice water stains on a ceiling the seller''s disclosure doesn''t mention. What should the agent do?', '["Tell the buyer it''s probably nothing","Say nothing because the seller didn''t disclose it","Point it out to the buyer and recommend a professional inspection","Ask the seller to paint over it"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Disclose material facts to your client and recommend experts for things you can''t evaluate.', '["Downplaying it without expertise is careless.","Keeping a material observation from your client breaches disclosure.","","Concealing defects is misrepresentation."]'::jsonb, 'Tell your client everything.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-buyer-client-defect', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Fiduciary duties are owed to clients, not to customers.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","Customers are owed honesty and fair dealing; clients get fiduciary duties."]'::jsonb, 'Clients get loyalty. Customers get honesty.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'fiduciary-to-clients-not-customers', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'The duty of obedience requires an agent to follow every instruction the client gives.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. Unlawful instructions must be refused.', '["Obedience applies only to lawful, ethical instructions.",""]'::jsonb, 'Obey the lawful. Refuse the unlawful.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'obedience-unlawful-exception', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'An agent may withhold a material fact from the client if sharing it might cost the agent a commission.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False.', '["Withholding material facts to protect a commission breaches both disclosure and loyalty.",""]'::jsonb, 'Client first, commission second.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-must-present-info-client', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'A listing agent''s sister wants to buy the agent''s listing. The agent should:', '["Refuse to present the offer","Keep the relationship private to stay neutral","Present it as a stranger''s offer","Disclose the relationship to the seller in writing before any offer is presented"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'A family relationship with a buyer is a conflict that must be disclosed to the client.', '["The seller should get to decide on every offer.","Hiding it is a conflict of interest.","Misrepresenting the buyer is fraud.",""]'::jsonb, 'If it benefits you, disclose it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'loyalty-relative-buyer', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A person authorized by a written power of attorney to act for someone else is called:', '["A remainderman","A trustee","An attorney-in-fact","An attorney-at-law"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'The holder of a power of attorney is an attorney-in-fact, who need not be a lawyer.', '["A remainderman receives a future interest.","A trustee holds title under a trust.","","An attorney-at-law is a licensed lawyer."]'::jsonb, 'In fact, not at law.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'poa-attorney-in-fact', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A buyer''s agent receives an earnest money check. Under the duty of accounting, the agent should:', '["Hold it in a desk drawer until closing","Give it to the seller","Deposit it in their personal account","Deliver it to the broker promptly for proper handling"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Client funds must be handed to the broker promptly and handled as trust money.', '["Holding it carelessly risks loss and breaks trust account rules.","Funds go through the proper trust process, not straight to the seller.","That''s commingling.",""]'::jsonb, 'Their money, separate account.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'accounting-earnest-promptly', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which is a material fact a seller''s agent must tell the seller?', '["The buyer''s favorite paint color","The buyer''s agent''s commission split with their broker","The buyer''s hometown","The buyer''s lender has questioned the buyer''s ability to qualify"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Information that could affect the deal, like doubts about financing, is material.', '["That doesn''t affect the seller''s decisions.","Internal splits generally don''t affect the seller''s decision.","That isn''t material.",""]'::jsonb, 'Material: it could change the decision.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'disclosure-client-material-facts', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'number', 1, 'calculation', 'A broker holds earnest money for three transactions: $5,000, $7,500, and $12,000. How much client money should the trust account show for these deposits?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":24500,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'The trust account must account for every client dollar: $24,500.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Accounting: every dollar tracked.', 'Total held = sum of all deposits', '["$5,000 + $7,500 = $12,500.","$12,500 + $12,000 = $24,500."]'::jsonb, null, 'accounting-deposits-total', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-17', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'scenario', 3, 'application', 'Your seller says, "Don''t mention the foundation crack. That''s an order." What should the agent do?', '["Tell buyers to skip the inspection","Explain you must disclose known material defects, and withdraw from the listing if the seller insists on hiding it","Obey, since obedience is a fiduciary duty","Disclose it only if a buyer asks directly"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Concealing a known material defect is misrepresentation. Refuse and, if necessary, withdraw.', '["That''s an attempt to conceal.","","Obedience doesn''t cover unlawful instructions.","Known material defects must be disclosed, asked or not."]'::jsonb, 'Obey the lawful. Refuse the unlawful.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-seller-hide-defect-instruction', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.3-18', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Recommending a home inspector or attorney when a question is outside the agent''s expertise is part of reasonable care.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","Referring to experts is how competent agents protect clients."]'::jsonb, 'Know your lane. Refer the rest.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'reasonable-care-refer-experts', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A listing agent says a home has "the most charming porch in the neighborhood." This is best described as:', '["Puffing","Negligent misrepresentation","Fraud","A material fact"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Exaggerated opinion that no reasonable buyer would treat as fact is puffing.', '["","It isn''t a factual claim made carelessly.","It''s an opinion, not an intentional false statement of fact.","\"Most charming\" isn''t a measurable fact."]'::jsonb, 'Opinion is puffing. False fact is trouble.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'puffing-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which is required for fraud?', '["Any statement the buyer later dislikes","An exaggerated opinion","An intentional false statement of a material fact that someone relies on and is harmed by","An honest mistake about square footage"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Fraud requires intent to deceive, materiality, reliance, and harm.', '["Disliking a statement isn''t fraud.","Opinion is puffing.","","An honest mistake may be negligence, not fraud."]'::jsonb, 'Fraud is a lie on purpose.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'fraud-elements', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'An agent advertises a home as 2,400 square feet based on a guess. It''s actually 1,950. The agent didn''t mean to deceive. This is most likely:', '["Fraud","Not a problem because there was no intent","Puffing","Negligent misrepresentation"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Stating a material fact carelessly, without reasonable verification, is negligent misrepresentation.', '["Fraud requires intent.","Careless false statements can still create liability.","Square footage is a fact, not an opinion.",""]'::jsonb, 'Careless facts still cost.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'negligent-misrep-sqft', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A defect hidden from ordinary inspection, like a crack in the slab under carpet, is a:', '["Functional obsolescence","Patent defect","Encroachment","Latent defect"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Latent defects can''t be seen by ordinary inspection and must be disclosed when known.', '["Functional obsolescence is a design flaw that lowers value.","A patent defect is visible.","An encroachment is an intrusion onto another''s land.",""]'::jsonb, 'Latent: hidden. Patent: plain to see.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'latent-defect-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A listing agent knows the AC compressor failed last week. A buyer the agent doesn''t represent asks if the AC works. The agent should:', '["Avoid answering","Say it works because the seller is the client","Tell the buyer to ask the inspector","Disclose that the compressor failed"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Licensees owe honesty to everyone and must disclose known material defects.', '["Silence about a known material defect isn''t allowed.","Lying to a customer is misrepresentation.","Deflecting a direct question about a known defect is concealment.",""]'::jsonb, 'Honest with everyone. Loyal to your client.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'known-defect-disclose-customer', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Today, caveat emptor ("let the buyer beware"):', '["Was never part of real estate law","Applies only to new construction","Is limited by disclosure laws and the licensee''s duty of honesty","Lets agents hide any defect"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Modern statutes and licensee duties largely replaced caveat emptor.', '["It was the traditional common-law rule.","It isn''t limited to new homes.","","Hiding known defects is misrepresentation."]'::jsonb, 'Buyer beware no longer means agent conceal.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'caveat-emptor-limited', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'A buyer you don''t represent asks whether they should take title as joint tenants with their partner. What should the agent do?', '["Explain you can''t give legal advice and suggest they ask an attorney","Tell them joint tenancy is always best","Tell them it doesn''t matter","Tell them to ask the seller"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'How to hold title is a legal question with lasting consequences. Refer it to an attorney.', '["","That''s legal advice, and wrong as a blanket rule.","How title is held has major legal effects.","The seller isn''t the right source."]'::jsonb, 'Know your lane. Refer the rest.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-no-legal-advice-customer', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'Asked about flooding, an agent says, "The seller has never filed a flood insurance claim." The agent knows the basement flooded twice and the seller paid for repairs out of pocket. This statement is:', '["A misrepresentation, because the half-truth hides a material fact","Puffing","Legal if the seller approved it","Fine, because it''s literally true"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Half-truths designed to mislead are misrepresentation.', '["","It''s a factual claim, not opinion.","Client approval doesn''t make concealment legal.","A technically true statement that creates a false impression can be misrepresentation."]'::jsonb, 'True words, false picture: still a lie.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'half-truth-misrep', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'A licensee owes honesty and fair dealing to all parties in a transaction, not just to clients.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","Honesty is owed to everyone."]'::jsonb, 'Honest with everyone.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-honesty-all-parties', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'A statement like "stunning sunset views" usually doesn''t create liability, as long as the home actually has views.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. Puffing is opinion; it becomes a problem only if it implies a false fact.', '["","Opinions about appeal are puffing; the underlying fact (there are views) must still be true."]'::jsonb, 'Opinion is puffing. False fact is trouble.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'puffing-not-liability', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Staying silent about a known material defect can never be a misrepresentation.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. Concealment by silence counts.', '["Concealing a known material fact through silence can be misrepresentation.",""]'::jsonb, 'Silence can lie too.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'silence-can-be-misrep', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A fact is "material" when:', '["It is written in the MLS","The seller considers it important","The buyer asks about it","It would affect a reasonable person''s decision to buy, sell, or set a price"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Materiality is judged by its effect on a reasonable person''s decision.', '["Being in the MLS doesn''t make a fact material.","The test is objective, not one person''s view.","Facts can be material whether or not anyone asks.",""]'::jsonb, 'Material: it could change the decision.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'material-fact-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'The seller tells you the home has a brand-new roof, but you see curling shingles. What should the agent do before advertising "new roof"?', '["Ask the buyer''s inspector to check after an offer","Advertise it because the seller said so","Advertise \"newer roof\" instead","Verify it, for example with a receipt or permit, or leave it out"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'When you have reason to doubt a fact, verify it before repeating it.', '["Waiting for the buyer to discover it is backwards.","Repeating a claim you have reason to doubt can be negligent.","Shading the wording doesn''t fix a doubtful fact.",""]'::jsonb, 'Doubt it? Verify it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-verify-before-advertise', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A seller falsely tells the agent the home has never had termites. The agent repeats it, having no reason to doubt it. Later the truth comes out. Generally:', '["The seller is liable; the agent''s exposure depends on whether they knew or should have known","The agent is always fully liable","Only the buyer''s agent is liable","No one is liable"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'The seller is liable for the lie. An agent is responsible when they knew or should have known the statement was false.', '["","Agents generally aren''t liable for false information they had no reason to doubt.","The buyer''s agent didn''t make the statement.","The seller who lied is liable."]'::jsonb, 'Knew or should have known: that''s the line.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-liable-repeat-seller-lie', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A large crack visible in the driveway is a:', '["Patent defect","Stigma","Lien","Latent defect"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'A visible defect is patent.', '["","A stigma is a non-physical issue like a crime.","A lien is a money claim.","Latent defects are hidden."]'::jsonb, 'Latent: hidden. Patent: plain to see.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'patent-defect-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'A buyer discovers after closing that the agent knowingly hid a severe sewer problem. Which remedy might the buyer pursue?', '["Nothing, because the sale closed","Only a new listing","Only a refund of the inspection fee","Damages or rescission of the sale, plus a complaint to the regulator"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Fraud can support damages or rescission, and licensees can face discipline.', '["Fraud can be pursued after closing.","A new listing isn''t a remedy.","Remedies aren''t limited to inspection fees.",""]'::jsonb, 'Hide it now, pay for it later.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'rescission-for-misrep', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-17', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'An agent may tell a buyer a crack is "just cosmetic" if the agent believes it, even without expertise.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False.', '["Giving expert-sounding opinions outside your expertise can be negligent misrepresentation. Recommend an expert.",""]'::jsonb, 'Know your lane. Refer the rest.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-no-expert-claims', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.4-18', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which is a licensee NOT required to do for a customer?', '["Advise them on negotiating strategy","Disclose known material defects","Account for the customer''s deposit","Answer questions honestly"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Negotiating advice is a client service. Customers get honesty, fairness and proper handling of money.', '["","Known material defects must be disclosed to all.","Funds received from anyone must be handled properly.","Honesty is owed to everyone."]'::jsonb, 'Clients get advice. Customers get honesty.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'fair-dealing-customer', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'The main purpose of agency disclosure is to:', '["Tell each party whom the licensee represents","Disclose property defects","Report the sale to the county","Set the commission"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Agency disclosure lets consumers know who works for whom before they share sensitive information.', '["","Defects are covered by property disclosures.","Recording is a different process.","Commission is set in the agency agreement."]'::jsonb, 'Say who you work for before they say too much.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agency-disclosure-purpose', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A listing agent wants to buy their own listing. The agent must:', '["Lower the price first","Wait until the listing expires, then buy quietly","Buy through a relative to avoid disclosure","Disclose in writing that they''re the buyer and get the seller''s informed consent"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'An agent buying a client''s property must fully disclose the interest and get informed consent.', '["Lowering the price for their own benefit is self-dealing.","Waiting doesn''t erase the conflict when the agent used inside knowledge.","Using a straw buyer to hide the interest is fraud.",""]'::jsonb, 'If it benefits you, disclose it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'licensee-buying-own-listing', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'An agent secretly accepts a $1,000 "bonus" from a contractor for steering clients to them. This is:', '["An allowed referral fee","A transaction fee","A secret profit and a breach of loyalty","Puffing"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Undisclosed benefits taken from a client''s transaction breach loyalty. Some kickbacks also violate RESPA.', '["Undisclosed payments for steering clients aren''t allowed referral fees.","It isn''t a disclosed fee.","","Puffing is exaggerated opinion."]'::jsonb, 'If it benefits you, disclose it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'secret-profit-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which is a likely consequence of undisclosed dual agency?', '["Nothing if the deal closes","Automatic approval by the regulator","A higher commission","Loss of the commission, discipline, and possible lawsuits"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Undisclosed dual agency breaches loyalty to both parties and carries serious penalties.', '["Closing doesn''t cure the violation.","Regulators discipline it.","No reward comes from it.",""]'::jsonb, 'Secret dual agency: two clients, zero loyalty.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'undisclosed-dual-consequences', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'You represent a buyer, and your own investment property is on the market and fits their needs. What should the agent do?', '["Disclose your ownership in writing before showing it, and let the buyer decide with full knowledge","Push it as the best option","Show it as if it belonged to a stranger","Never mention it"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'A personal interest in a property is a conflict that must be disclosed before proceeding.', '["","Pushing your own property puts your interests first.","Hiding ownership is self-dealing.","Your client might benefit from seeing it; disclosure, not secrecy, is the answer."]'::jsonb, 'If it benefits you, disclose it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-conflict-own-buyer', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A salesperson receives a referral fee for sending a client to an out-of-state agent. Generally, the fee must be:', '["Paid through the salesperson''s broker and disclosed as required","Refused, because referral fees are always illegal","Paid directly to the salesperson in cash","Kept secret from the client"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Licensee compensation, including referral fees, flows through the broker, with disclosure as the law requires.', '["","Referral fees between licensees are generally allowed with proper handling.","Salespeople are paid through their broker.","Required disclosures can''t be skipped."]'::jsonb, 'All pay flows through the broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'referral-fee-through-broker', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'Acting with informed written consent as a dual agent, a licensee generally must not:', '["Tell the buyer the seller''s lowest acceptable price","Prepare paperwork","Disclose known defects","Present offers"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'A dual agent can''t reveal one party''s confidential negotiating position to the other.', '["","Paperwork is a normal task.","Disclosing defects is required.","Presenting offers is allowed."]'::jsonb, 'Two clients, two sets of secrets.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'dual-agent-limits', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'A licensee buying or selling property for themselves should disclose that they hold a real estate license.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. The other party should know they''re dealing with a professional.', '["","Licensees dealing for themselves must disclose their license status, as state law sets out."]'::jsonb, 'Licensed? Say so.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'disclose-licensee-status-own-deal', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Where dual agency is allowed, a quick verbal "OK" from each party is usually enough consent.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False.', '["Dual agency typically requires informed written consent on the state''s required form.",""]'::jsonb, 'Two clients, one firm: disclose in writing and get consent.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'dual-agency-oral-consent', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Agency relationships should be disclosed:', '["Early, before the consumer shares confidential information, as state law requires","Only at closing","Only if someone asks","After the offer is accepted"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Timely disclosure protects consumers before they reveal their position.', '["","Too late to protect the consumer.","Disclosure isn''t optional.","By then confidential information may already be shared."]'::jsonb, 'Say who you work for before they say too much.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'disclosure-timing-early', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'Your brokerage co-owns the title company you recommend to clients. You should:', '["Tell clients you have no connection","Disclose the business relationship to your clients as the law requires","Hide it so clients don''t worry","Require clients to use it"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Affiliated business relationships must be disclosed; federal RESPA requires a written disclosure for affiliated settlement services.', '["That would be false.","","Hiding it violates disclosure rules, and RESPA has specific requirements for affiliated businesses.","Clients choose their own service providers."]'::jsonb, 'If it benefits you, disclose it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'vendor-relationship-disclose', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'scenario', 3, 'application', 'Two of your buyer clients want to make offers on the same house. What should the agent do?', '["Tell each buyer what the other is offering","Disclose the situation to both clients, follow your broker''s policy, and keep each client''s offer terms confidential from the other","Help only the buyer offering more commission","Secretly favor the first client"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Competing clients create a conflict. Disclose it, protect each client''s confidential information, and follow brokerage policy.', '["Sharing one client''s terms with another breaches confidentiality.","","Choosing by commission breaches loyalty.","Secret favoritism is a breach to the second client."]'::jsonb, 'Two clients, two sets of secrets.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-two-buyers-same-house', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Putting conflict-of-interest disclosures in writing protects both the client and the licensee.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","Written disclosures create a clear record."]'::jsonb, 'If it isn''t written, it''s hard to prove.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'conflicts-disclosed-in-writing', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Under federal RESPA, a licensee accepting a fee from a lender just for referring a borrower is:', '["Allowed if under $500","Generally prohibited as a kickback","Required by law","Allowed if disclosed verbally"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'RESPA prohibits fees or things of value given for referrals of settlement service business.', '["There''s no dollar exemption for kickbacks.","","Nothing requires it.","Verbal disclosure doesn''t make a kickback legal."]'::jsonb, 'Paid just for the referral? That''s a kickback.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'kickback-respa', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'After closing, a happy seller sends the agent a $50 gift card. Generally this is:', '["A secret profit","Illegal for any licensee","Acceptable, if brokerage policy allows and nothing was promised in return","A RESPA kickback"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'A small post-closing gift from your own client isn''t a secret profit, though brokerage policy may control.', '["A secret profit comes from a third party in a client''s transaction without the client''s knowledge; this is from the client.","Small thank-you gifts from clients aren''t automatically illegal.","","RESPA targets referral payments between settlement service providers."]'::jsonb, 'From the client, after the deal, nothing promised: usually fine.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-gift-from-client-ok', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Disclosing a conflict of interest means the agent can then act against the client''s interest.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False.', '["Disclosure lets the client make an informed choice. It never permits acting against the client.",""]'::jsonb, 'Disclosure informs; it doesn''t excuse.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'disclosure-not-cure-all', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-17', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Informed consent to dual agency generally means the parties understand:', '["That the licensee represents both, and how that limits what the licensee can do for each","Only the listing price","Nothing, as long as they sign","Only the commission amount"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'The parties must understand the dual role and its limits before consenting.', '["","Price isn''t the key issue.","A signature without understanding isn''t informed consent.","Commission isn''t the key issue."]'::jsonb, 'Consent means understanding, not just a signature.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'dual-agency-informed-consent-elements', 'unverified'),
  ('N5.5-18', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N5', 'N5.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'AGY', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'Your buyer''s inspection reveals serious problems, and the buyer is unsure. Your rent is due, and you need this commission. What should the agent do?', '["Downplay the problems so the deal closes","Suggest skipping the repair request","Give the buyer an objective picture of the findings and options, and support whatever decision is best for them","Tell the buyer the deadline has passed when it hasn''t"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Loyalty means the client''s interests come first, even when it costs you a commission.', '["That puts your commission ahead of your client.","Steering the client to benefit yourself breaches loyalty.","","Lying about deadlines is misrepresentation."]'::jsonb, 'Client first, commission second.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-pressure-to-close-commission', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Which list contains only essential elements of a valid contract?', '["Competent parties, offer and acceptance, consideration, legal purpose","Competent parties, notarization, recording, legal purpose","Offer, earnest money, title insurance, consideration","Written form, recording, consideration, broker signature"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Every valid contract needs competent parties, mutual assent through offer and acceptance, consideration, and a legal purpose.', '["","Notarization and recording are not required for a contract to be valid.","Earnest money and title insurance are common but not essential elements.","Recording and a broker''s signature are not essential elements."]'::jsonb, 'COAL: Competent, Offer and acceptance, consideration, Legal.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'contract-essential-elements', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Under the statute of frauds, a contract for the sale of real estate must be:', '["Notarized by both parties","Recorded with the county","In writing and signed by the party to be charged","Approved by the Real Estate Division"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'The statute of frauds makes contracts to sell land enforceable only if they are written and signed.', '["Notarization is needed to record a deed, not to make a sale contract enforceable.","Recording gives public notice but isn''t what makes the contract enforceable.","","The Division does not approve individual sale contracts."]'::jsonb, 'Land deals live on paper.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'statute-of-frauds-real-estate', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A 17-year-old signs a contract to buy a condo. The contract is:', '["Voidable by the minor","Voidable by the seller","Void from the start","Fully enforceable against both parties"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Contracts with minors are voidable at the minor''s option. The adult party is still bound.', '["","Only the minor, the protected party, has the right to cancel.","A minor''s contract isn''t void. It stands unless the minor chooses to cancel.","The minor can disaffirm the contract."]'::jsonb, 'Voidable is the protected party''s choice.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'minor-contract-voidable', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A contract to lease a building for an illegal gambling operation is:', '["Voidable","Valid if both parties signed","Void","Unenforceable but valid"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'A contract with an illegal purpose is void. It has no legal effect from the start.', '["Voidable contracts are valid until someone cancels; an illegal purpose means there was never a contract.","Signatures can''t make an illegal purpose legal.","","A contract with an illegal purpose isn''t valid at all."]'::jsonb, 'Void is nothing.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'void-illegal-purpose', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'Two neighbors agree out loud on a price for a vacant lot and shake hands. The agreement is best described as:', '["Unenforceable","Voidable","Executed","Void"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'An oral contract to sell land may be valid between the parties, but under the statute of frauds a court won''t enforce it.', '["","Voidable means one protected party may cancel; that isn''t the problem here.","Executed means fully performed; nothing has been performed.","It isn''t void; the elements may exist, but a court won''t enforce it without a writing."]'::jsonb, 'Land deals live on paper.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'oral-land-contract-unenforceable', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A purchase agreement in which the buyer promises to pay and the seller promises to convey is a:', '["Implied contract","Void contract","Bilateral contract","Unilateral contract"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'When both parties exchange promises, the contract is bilateral.', '["The terms are stated in words, so it''s express, not implied.","Nothing here makes it void.","","In a unilateral contract only one party promises."]'::jsonb, 'Bi means both promise.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'bilateral-purchase-agreement', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A signed purchase agreement that hasn''t closed yet is:', '["Executory","Executed","Void","Unilateral"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'A contract that still has obligations to be performed is executory.', '["","Executed means fully performed, which happens at closing.","A signed agreement meeting all elements isn''t void.","Both parties made promises, so it''s bilateral."]'::jsonb, 'Executory: the work is still in the story.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'executory-before-closing', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A broker starts showing a buyer homes, the buyer accepts the help, and both act as if the broker represents the buyer, though nothing was said or written. This may create a(n):', '["Unilateral option","Express contract","Novation","Implied contract"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Conduct alone can create an implied contract, including an implied agency.', '["An option gives a right to buy on set terms; that isn''t happening here.","An express contract is stated in words.","Novation replaces an existing contract.",""]'::jsonb, 'Actions can sign a contract too.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'implied-contract-conduct', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'A buyer calls you and says, "Tell the seller I''ll pay $380,000. We don''t need paperwork." What should the agent do?', '["Tell the seller the buyer has made a binding offer","Call the seller and accept on the buyer''s behalf","Explain that an offer to buy real estate must be in writing and prepare a written offer for the buyer to sign","Wait to see if the seller calls back"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Real estate contracts must be in writing to be enforceable. Put the offer in writing and have the buyer sign it.', '["An oral offer to buy land isn''t enforceable, so calling it binding misleads the seller.","The agent can''t accept anything for the buyer, and there''s no seller acceptance to give.","","Doing nothing fails the buyer."]'::jsonb, 'Land deals live on paper.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-oral-offer-writing', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A seller signs a contract only because the buyer threatened them. The contract is:', '["Void","Fully enforceable","Voidable by the seller","Voidable by the buyer"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Duress, menace, fraud, and undue influence make a contract voidable by the injured party.', '["Duress makes a contract voidable, not void.","A party forced to sign can cancel.","","The buyer caused the duress and has no right to cancel."]'::jsonb, 'Forced to sign? Free to cancel.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'duress-voidable', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Consideration in a contract must always be money.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. A promise, an act, or property can be consideration.', '["Consideration can be anything of legal value, including a promise or an act.",""]'::jsonb, 'A promise can pay for a promise.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'consideration-not-only-money', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'In a unilateral contract, only one party makes a promise.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. The other party can accept only by performing the requested act.', '["","That''s exactly what makes it unilateral: a promise in exchange for an act."]'::jsonb, 'Uni means one promises.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'unilateral-one-promise', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'A purchase agreement must be recorded with the county to be valid.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. Recording isn''t an element of a valid contract.', '["Recording gives public notice. It isn''t required for the contract to be valid between the parties.",""]'::jsonb, 'Recording warns the world. It doesn''t make the deal.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'contract-need-not-be-recorded', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', '"Meeting of the minds" refers to which contract element?', '["Offer and acceptance","Competent parties","Consideration","Legal purpose"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Mutual assent, shown by offer and acceptance, is the meeting of the minds.', '["","Competency concerns who can contract.","Consideration is what each party gives.","Legal purpose concerns what the contract is for."]'::jsonb, 'Minds meet when an offer is accepted.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'mutual-assent-meeting-of-minds', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'After closing, a buyer says the seller orally promised to leave the hot tub, but the signed contract lists the included items and doesn''t mention it. Under the parol evidence rule, generally:', '["The buyer automatically gets the hot tub","Both are equally binding","The written contract controls over earlier oral statements","The oral promise controls because it came first"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'The parol evidence rule generally bars earlier or same-time oral statements from changing a complete written contract.', '["Without a written term, the buyer has no automatic right to it.","Courts generally won''t let earlier oral terms contradict a complete written contract.","","The rule works the opposite way: the final writing wins."]'::jsonb, 'Get it in the paper, or it isn''t in the deal.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'parol-evidence-rule', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.1-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.1', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A contract that both parties have fully performed is:', '["Voidable","Bilateral only","Executed","Executory"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'An executed contract has been completely performed.', '["Voidable concerns a right to cancel, not performance.","Bilateral describes the promises, not whether they''re performed.","","Executory means performance is still due."]'::jsonb, 'Executed: done and dusted.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'executed-contract-performed', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A buyer assigns their purchase contract to a friend. Unless released, the original buyer:', '["Remains liable if the friend fails to perform","Is released automatically","Must record the assignment to be released","Becomes the seller''s agent"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'In an assignment the assignor usually stays secondarily liable unless the other party agrees to a release.', '["","Automatic release happens with novation, not assignment.","Recording doesn''t release anyone.","Assignment creates no agency relationship."]'::jsonb, 'Assign and you still sign for it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'assignment-original-liable', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Substituting a new party for an original party and releasing the original party is called:', '["Novation","Subordination","Rescission","Assignment"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Novation replaces a party or contract and releases the old one.', '["","Subordination changes lien priority.","Rescission cancels the contract altogether.","Assignment doesn''t release the original party."]'::jsonb, 'Novation sets you free.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'novation-releases', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A seller refuses to close because a higher offer came in. Which remedy best fits a buyer who wants the property itself?', '["Liquidated damages","Rescission","Novation","Specific performance"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Because land is unique, a court may order the seller to perform and convey the property.', '["Liquidated damages pay money, not the property.","Rescission undoes the contract, the opposite of what the buyer wants.","Novation substitutes a party; it isn''t a breach remedy.",""]'::jsonb, 'Land is unique, so courts can make you sell.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'specific-performance-buyer', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A purchase agreement says that if the buyer defaults, the seller keeps the earnest money as full damages. This is a:', '["Specific performance clause","Contingency","Novation","Liquidated damages clause"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'An amount agreed in advance as damages for breach is liquidated damages.', '["Specific performance would force the buyer to buy, not set money damages.","A contingency is a condition, not a damages agreement.","Novation substitutes a contract or party.",""]'::jsonb, 'Liquidated: damages settled ahead of time.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'liquidated-damages-earnest', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Buyer and seller both agree to cancel their contract and return the deposit. This is:', '["Specific performance","Breach","Mutual rescission","Assignment"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Both parties agreeing to cancel and restore each other to their original positions is mutual rescission.', '["Specific performance enforces a contract.","No one failed to perform; they agreed to end it.","","Assignment transfers rights to someone else."]'::jsonb, 'Rescind: rewind the deal.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'mutual-rescission', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A contract says "time is of the essence" and requires closing by May 15. The buyer is ready on May 18. Most likely:', '["The deadline automatically extends 30 days","The buyer is in breach for missing the deadline","Three days late is acceptable","The contract converts to an option"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'A "time is of the essence" clause makes deadlines strictly enforceable, so missing one is a breach.', '["Nothing extends the deadline automatically.","","With time of the essence, deadlines are strict.","Missing a deadline doesn''t create an option."]'::jsonb, 'When time is of the essence, late is broken.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'time-of-essence-deadline', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'The law that limits how long a party has to file a lawsuit for breach of contract is the:', '["Statute of frauds","Statute of limitations","Parol evidence rule","Doctrine of laches only"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Each state sets time limits for filing suits; that''s the statute of limitations.', '["The statute of frauds requires certain contracts to be in writing.","","The parol evidence rule limits oral evidence about written contracts.","Laches is a related idea about unreasonable delay, but the time limit set by law is the statute of limitations."]'::jsonb, 'Limitations: the clock on lawsuits.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'statute-of-limitations-def', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Money awarded to cover the actual loss caused by a breach is called:', '["Specific performance","Compensatory damages","Liquidated damages","Consideration"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Compensatory damages make the injured party whole for actual losses.', '["Specific performance orders performance, not money.","","Liquidated damages are set in advance in the contract.","Consideration is what parties exchange to form a contract."]'::jsonb, 'Compensate the loss.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'compensatory-damages-def', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'Before closing, a wildfire destroys the home and the contract says the risk of loss stays with the seller. The buyer may most likely:', '["Cancel the contract and get the earnest money back","Sue the listing broker for the loss","Keep the contract open forever","Be forced to close at full price"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'When the seller bears the risk of loss and the property is destroyed, the buyer can generally cancel and recover the deposit.', '["","The broker didn''t cause the fire.","There''s no basis to hold it open indefinitely.","The contract puts the risk on the seller, so the buyer isn''t forced to buy a destroyed home."]'::jsonb, 'Read who carries the risk before the fire.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'operation-of-law-impossibility', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'Your seller asks whether they can sue the buyer who walked away two days before closing. What should the agent do?', '["Explain the contract terms they can see, and recommend the seller talk to a real estate attorney about legal remedies","Tell the seller nothing can be done","Tell the seller exactly how much they will win in court","Draft a lawsuit for the seller"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Agents can point to contract terms but must refer legal questions about remedies to an attorney.', '["","That''s false and could cost the seller rights they have.","Predicting legal outcomes is legal advice the agent isn''t licensed to give.","Drafting legal pleadings is the practice of law."]'::jsonb, 'Point to the paper, refer the law.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-breach-refer-attorney', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Most real estate contracts can be assigned unless the contract prohibits assignment.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. Assignment is allowed unless the contract forbids it or it''s a personal service contract.', '["","Contracts are generally assignable unless they say otherwise or involve personal services."]'::jsonb, 'Assignable unless it says no.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'assignable-unless-prohibited', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Personal service contracts, such as a listing agreement, can generally be assigned to any broker without the owner''s consent.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. Personal service contracts generally can''t be assigned without consent.', '["The owner hired a specific broker, so personal service contracts generally can''t be assigned without consent.",""]'::jsonb, 'You hired a person, not a placeholder.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'listing-not-assignable-personal', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Rescission returns the parties to their positions before the contract was made.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. Rescission unwinds the contract.', '["","That''s the purpose of rescission."]'::jsonb, 'Rescind: rewind the deal.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'rescission-restores-positions', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A buyer put down 3% earnest money on a $420,000 purchase. The contract makes the earnest money the seller''s liquidated damages. The buyer defaults. How much does the seller keep?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":12600,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'The seller keeps the agreed liquidated damages: 3% of $420,000, which is $12,600.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Liquidated: damages settled ahead of time.', 'Earnest money = price × earnest money percent', '["Convert 3% to a decimal: 0.03.","$420,000 × 0.03 = $12,600."]'::jsonb, null, 'liquidated-damages-calc', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Failing, without a legal excuse, to do what a contract requires is:', '["A novation","A rescission","A breach","An assignment"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Nonperformance without a legal excuse is a breach of contract.', '["Novation substitutes a new contract or party.","Rescission is canceling by agreement or right.","","Assignment transfers rights."]'::jsonb, 'No excuse, no performance: breach.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'breach-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.2-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.2', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'A seller agreed to repaint the house before closing but used a slightly different shade of white. A court is most likely to treat this as:', '["Fraud","A total breach that cancels the sale","A novation","Substantial performance, possibly with a small damages adjustment"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'When performance is essentially complete with a minor deviation, courts often find substantial performance.', '["Nothing suggests intent to deceive.","A trivial deviation usually isn''t enough to cancel the whole contract.","No new contract or party was substituted.",""]'::jsonb, 'Close enough counts, minus the difference.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'substantial-performance', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Under an exclusive right to sell listing, the owner finds a buyer with no help from the broker. The broker is:', '["Entitled to the commission","Owed only expenses","Owed half the commission","Owed nothing"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'In an exclusive right to sell, the broker is paid no matter who sells.', '["","The broker is owed the full agreed commission, not just expenses.","Nothing in this listing type splits the commission when the owner sells.","That''s the exclusive agency rule, not exclusive right to sell."]'::jsonb, 'Right to sell means the right to be paid.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'exclusive-right-owner-sells', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Under an exclusive agency listing, the owner sells the home to a coworker without any broker. The broker is:', '["Owed commission only if the sale closes","Owed a referral fee by law","Owed the full commission","Owed no commission"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'An exclusive agency listing lets the owner sell without paying the broker.', '["Closing doesn''t matter; the owner found the buyer.","No law requires a referral fee here.","The owner kept the right to sell without paying.",""]'::jsonb, 'Exclusive agency: the owner keeps one exit.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'exclusive-agency-owner-sells', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'An owner gives open listings to three brokers. Who earns a commission?', '["The first broker to list it","No broker, because open listings don''t pay","Only the broker who is the procuring cause of the sale","All three brokers equally"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'With open listings, only the procuring cause of the sale is paid.', '["Listing first doesn''t decide who''s paid.","Open listings do pay the procuring broker.","","Only the broker who produces the buyer is paid."]'::jsonb, 'Open listing: the one who brings the buyer gets paid.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'open-listing-procuring-cause', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Why are net listings illegal or discouraged in many states?', '["They are always unwritten","They create a conflict of interest between the broker and the seller over the price","They require a dual agent","They can''t be placed in the MLS"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Because the broker keeps everything above the seller''s net, the broker benefits from a sale price the seller may not understand.', '["Net listings can be written; that isn''t the issue.","","Net listings don''t require dual agency.","MLS rules aren''t the reason they''re discouraged."]'::jsonb, 'Net listing: the agent''s gain is the seller''s pain.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'net-listing-conflict', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A listing expired June 1. On June 20 the owner sells directly to a buyer the broker showed the home to in May, and the listing has a 90-day protection clause. The broker is most likely:', '["Owed nothing unless the MLS is notified","Owed half","Entitled to the commission","Owed nothing because the listing expired"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'A protection (safety) clause pays the broker if a buyer they introduced buys within the protection period.', '["MLS notice isn''t the trigger.","The clause doesn''t create a split.","","The protection clause covers buyers introduced during the listing."]'::jsonb, 'Introduced it? You''re protected.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'protection-clause-apply', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which event terminates a listing agreement by operation of law?', '["A price reduction","The death of the seller","The seller''s change of address","A showing with no offer"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Listings are personal service contracts, so the death or incapacity of either party ends them.', '["Changing the price amends the listing; it doesn''t end it.","","Moving doesn''t end a listing.","A showing doesn''t affect the listing."]'::jsonb, 'Personal contract: if a person goes, the listing goes.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'listing-ends-death', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A listing agreement is best described as:', '["A contract to sell the property to the broker","A lease","A deed","An employment contract between the owner and the broker"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'A listing hires the broker to find a buyer; it''s an employment contract.', '["The broker is hired to market, not to buy.","A lease grants possession.","A deed transfers title.",""]'::jsonb, 'A listing hires the broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'listing-employment-contract', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A salesperson takes a listing and then changes brokerages. The listing generally:', '["Is canceled","Moves with the salesperson automatically","Becomes an open listing","Stays with the original broker"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'The listing contract belongs to the broker, so it stays with the brokerage.', '["Changing firms doesn''t cancel the broker''s contract.","Listings are contracts with the broker, not the salesperson.","Nothing converts it to an open listing.",""]'::jsonb, 'Listings belong to the broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'listing-belongs-to-broker', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'A seller says, "Just get me $300,000 net and keep anything above that." What should the agent do?', '["List it at $300,000 and buy it themselves","Agree and list at the highest price the market will bear","Agree but keep the arrangement off paper","Explain the conflict of interest, decline a net arrangement, and set a commission and list price the seller understands"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'A net listing pits the agent against the seller. Use a clear commission and a price based on market data.', '["Buying the listing without full disclosure and the seller''s informed consent is self-dealing.","That''s a net listing with a built-in conflict.","Hiding the arrangement makes the problem worse.",""]'::jsonb, 'Net listing: the agent''s gain is the seller''s pain.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-seller-wants-net-listing', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Procuring cause means the broker whose efforts started an unbroken chain of events leading to the sale.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","That''s the standard meaning of procuring cause."]'::jsonb, 'Procuring cause started the chain.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'procuring-cause-definition', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'A salesperson can enter into a listing agreement in their own name, separate from their broker.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. Listings are taken in the broker''s name.', '["Salespeople act on the broker''s behalf; listings are the broker''s contracts.",""]'::jsonb, 'Listings belong to the broker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'salesperson-cannot-hold-listing', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'A listing can end by operation of law if the property is destroyed.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","Destruction of the property, death, incapacity, and bankruptcy can end a listing by law."]'::jsonb, 'No property, no listing.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'bankruptcy-ends-listing', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'The main purpose of a multiple listing service is to:', '["Let member brokers share listings and cooperate","Record deeds","Set commission rates for members","License real estate agents"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'An MLS is a cooperative system for sharing listing information among members.', '["","The county records deeds.","Setting commissions as a group would be price fixing.","The state licenses agents."]'::jsonb, 'MLS: many brokers, one list.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'mls-purpose', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'Halfway through an exclusive right to sell listing, the seller fires the broker for no reason. Generally:', '["The seller can''t end the agency under any circumstances","The seller can end the agency but may owe damages for breaching the contract","The broker must keep marketing the home","The listing converts to an open listing"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'The seller has the power to revoke the agency, but without cause they may be liable for the broker''s damages.', '["A principal can revoke an agency, though it may be a breach.","","Once the agency is revoked, the broker can''t act for the seller.","Nothing converts it automatically."]'::jsonb, 'You can fire your agent; you may have to pay for it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'seller-cancel-listing-liability', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'Your seller is about to sign an exclusive right to sell listing and asks what happens if their cousin buys the house. What should the agent do?', '["Explain that under this listing the commission is owed even if the cousin buys, and offer to discuss excluding the cousin in writing if appropriate","Say the cousin sale wouldn''t count","Tell them to sign an open listing with the cousin","Avoid the question until after they sign"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Explain the listing terms honestly before signing. Named exclusions must be in writing.', '["","That''s wrong for an exclusive right to sell.","Advising a separate listing with a non-broker makes no sense.","Hiding material terms violates the agent''s duty of disclosure."]'::jsonb, 'Right to sell means the right to be paid.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-listing-terms-explain', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.3-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.3', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A home listed under an exclusive right to sell at 5.5% commission sells for $510,000. What is the total commission?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":28050,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '$510,000 × 0.055 = $28,050.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Price times rate equals commission.', 'Commission = sale price × commission rate', '["5.5% = 0.055.","$510,000 × 0.055 = $28,050."]'::jsonb, null, 'listing-commission-calc', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A buyer agency agreement mainly:', '["Guarantees the buyer will find a home","Obligates the seller to pay the buyer''s broker","Transfers title to the buyer","Creates an agency relationship and states the broker''s duties and pay"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'The buyer agreement sets up the agency and spells out duties, term, and compensation.', '["No agreement can guarantee an outcome.","The seller isn''t a party to the buyer''s agreement.","Only a deed transfers title.",""]'::jsonb, 'Put the buyer''s relationship on paper.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-agency-creates-relationship', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Under an exclusive buyer agency agreement, the buyer finds and buys a home on their own during the term. The broker is generally:', '["Owed a referral fee by the seller","Owed nothing","Entitled to compensation","Owed compensation only if they showed that home"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'An exclusive buyer agreement usually pays the broker if the buyer purchases during the term, however the home was found.', '["The seller has no agreement with the buyer''s broker.","Exclusive means the broker is paid if the buyer buys during the term.","","Showing the specific home isn''t required under an exclusive agreement."]'::jsonb, 'Exclusive means one broker, paid either way.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'exclusive-buyer-agency-paid', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Under a nonexclusive buyer agreement, a broker is usually paid only if:', '["The seller agrees","The buyer buys anything during the term","The buyer gets a loan","The broker is the procuring cause of the purchase"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Nonexclusive agreements let buyers use other brokers, so payment follows procuring cause.', '["The seller''s agreement isn''t the trigger.","That describes an exclusive agreement.","Financing isn''t the trigger.",""]'::jsonb, 'Nonexclusive: bring the deal, get paid.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'nonexclusive-buyer-procuring', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A buyer agreement promises the broker 2.5%. The seller offers buyer brokers 2%. Under a typical agreement, the remaining 0.5%:', '["Is paid by the title company","Must be paid by the listing agent","May be owed by the buyer, as the agreement states","Is waived automatically"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'The buyer agreement controls the buyer broker''s compensation; if the seller pays less, the buyer may owe the difference.', '["Title companies don''t owe commissions.","The listing agent isn''t party to the buyer agreement.","","Nothing waives it unless the agreement says so."]'::jsonb, 'Who pays, how much, and when: write it down.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-pays-difference', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'A buyer wants to tour homes today and asks what they''re signing in your buyer agreement. What should the agent do?', '["Walk through the term, the duties, and exactly how and how much the broker will be paid, and answer questions before they sign","Let them tour first and explain the agreement after they''ve chosen a home","Tell them the seller always pays so the terms don''t matter","Say it''s a standard form and they don''t need to read it"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'The buyer should understand the agreement, especially compensation, before signing.', '["","Material terms belong at the start, not after decisions are made.","That''s not always true and misstates the agreement.","Waving off a contract''s terms fails the duty to disclose."]'::jsonb, 'Explain it before they sign it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-explain-buyer-agreement', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which term is most important to include so a buyer agreement doesn''t run forever?', '["The listing broker''s name","The home''s legal description","A definite expiration date","The buyer''s credit score"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'A clear expiration date defines how long the relationship and obligations last.', '["The buyer agreement isn''t tied to one listing.","No specific home is known when it''s signed.","","Credit details don''t set the term."]'::jsonb, 'Every agreement needs an end date.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-agreement-term-date', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A business hires a broker to find office space to lease. The agreement is best called a:', '["Option to purchase","Property management agreement","Tenant representation agreement","Exclusive right to sell listing"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Tenant representation agreements hire a broker to represent someone seeking to lease.', '["An option gives a right to buy on set terms.","Property management is for owners, not tenants.","","That''s for selling property."]'::jsonb, 'Tenants can hire representation too.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'tenant-rep-agreement', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'A buyer agreement expires March 1. On March 20 the buyer buys a home the broker showed in February, and the agreement has a 60-day protection clause. The broker is most likely:', '["Owed compensation under the agreement","Owed only if the buyer re-signs","Owed compensation only from the seller","Owed nothing because it expired"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Like listings, buyer agreements often include a protection period for properties shown during the term.', '["","No new signature is needed for the protection clause to apply.","Who pays depends on the agreement; the buyer may owe it.","The protection period covers homes shown during the term."]'::jsonb, 'Introduced it? You''re protected.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-agreement-protection-period', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'A buyer''s broker can be paid by the seller and still represent the buyer.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. Agency depends on the relationship, not the source of payment.', '["","Who pays does not determine whom the broker represents."]'::jsonb, 'Payment doesn''t decide loyalty.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-broker-can-be-paid-by-seller', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'Relying on an oral buyer agreement makes it easier for a broker to collect compensation in a dispute.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. Written agreements make terms provable and enforceable.', '["Oral agreements are hard to prove and may be unenforceable for commissions. Written agreements protect everyone.",""]'::jsonb, 'If it isn''t written, it''s hard to collect.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-agreement-oral-risky', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Once a buyer agency agreement is signed, the broker owes the buyer:', '["Duties only if the seller agrees","Fiduciary duties","Only honesty, the same as any customer","Nothing until closing"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'The buyer becomes the broker''s client, owed fiduciary duties.', '["The seller''s consent isn''t needed.","","A client is owed more than a customer: full fiduciary duties.","Duties begin when the agency begins."]'::jsonb, 'Sign the agreement, gain a client.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-agency-fiduciary', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A buyer agreement promises the broker 2.5% of the price. The home sells for $460,000 and the seller pays the buyer''s broker 2%. How much does the buyer owe the broker to make up the difference?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":2300,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'The gap is 0.5% of $460,000, which is $2,300.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Who pays, how much, and when: write it down.', 'Shortfall = price × (agreed rate − rate paid by seller)', '["2.5% − 2% = 0.5% = 0.005.","$460,000 × 0.005 = $2,300."]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-shortfall-calc', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A represented buyer loves a for-sale-by-owner home. The buyer''s broker should:', '["Help the buyer pursue it and resolve compensation as the buyer agreement provides","Refuse to show it because no commission is offered","Ask the seller to sign an exclusive right to sell listing first","Tell the buyer it''s illegal to buy without a listing"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'A buyer''s broker serves the buyer. The buyer agreement covers compensation when the seller pays nothing.', '["","Steering a client away from a home over commission puts the broker''s interests first.","The buyer''s broker doesn''t need a listing to help the buyer.","Buying from an owner directly is legal."]'::jsonb, 'The client''s interest comes before the commission.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-agent-show-fsbo', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Like a listing, a buyer agency agreement ends:', '["Only when the broker dies","On performance, expiration, mutual agreement, or by operation of law","Only when the buyer closes","Never, once signed"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Agency agreements end the same ways: performance, expiration, agreement, or operation of law.', '["Death of either party is just one way.","","There are several ways it can end besides closing.","Agreements always have ways to end."]'::jsonb, 'Every agreement has an exit.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-agreement-termination', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Compensation in a buyer agreement is negotiable between the buyer and the broker.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. Commissions are set by negotiation, not by law or by groups of brokers.', '["","Commissions are always negotiable; no law sets them."]'::jsonb, 'Every commission is negotiable.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'buyer-agreement-negotiable', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.4-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.4', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A buyer under an exclusive agreement wants to see a home listed by the same brokerage. Before going further, the brokerage must:', '["Refuse to show the home","Disclose the relationship and get the required informed consent from both parties","Cancel the buyer agreement","Ask the seller to cancel the listing"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Representing both sides requires disclosure and informed consent, as state law sets out.', '["Refusing isn''t required; consent and disclosure are.","","There''s no need to cancel; disclosure and consent are the path forward.","The listing doesn''t need to be canceled."]'::jsonb, 'Two clients, one firm: disclose and get consent.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'dual-agency-buyer-agreement-disclosure', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A seller responds to an offer by changing only the closing date. Legally, the seller has:', '["Made a binding contract with a new date","Created an option","Accepted the offer","Rejected the offer and made a counteroffer"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Any change is a counteroffer, which rejects the original offer.', '["No contract exists until the buyer accepts the new terms.","An option is a separate contract.","Acceptance must match the offer exactly.",""]'::jsonb, 'Change anything, and you''ve rejected everything.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'counteroffer-rejects-original', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A buyer can withdraw an offer:', '["Never, once it''s in writing","Only after the inspection","Any time before acceptance is communicated","Only with the seller''s permission"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'An offer can be revoked before the offeror learns it has been accepted.', '["A written offer can still be revoked before acceptance.","Inspection timing has nothing to do with revocation.","","The offeror controls the offer until acceptance."]'::jsonb, 'No acceptance yet? Still yours to take back.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'offer-revoked-before-acceptance', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'After signing a purchase agreement but before closing, the buyer holds:', '["Equitable title","A life estate","No interest at all","Legal title"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'A buyer under contract holds equitable title until legal title passes at closing.', '["","A life estate is a freehold measured by a life.","The buyer has an enforceable interest.","Legal title passes at closing by deed."]'::jsonb, 'Signed contract: equitable now, legal later.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'equitable-title-buyer', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'Earnest money is best described as:', '["A required down payment set by law","The broker''s commission","A good-faith deposit held in trust and usually credited to the buyer at closing","A fee paid to the seller that''s never refunded"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Earnest money shows good faith, is held in trust, and is usually applied to the buyer''s costs at closing.', '["No law sets a required amount.","It belongs to the transaction, not the broker.","","It''s often refundable if a contingency isn''t met."]'::jsonb, 'Earnest money: proof you''re serious.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'earnest-money-purpose', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A buyer with a financing contingency is denied a loan despite applying in good faith. Usually the buyer can:', '["Lose the earnest money","Be sued for specific performance","Be forced to pay cash","Cancel and get the earnest money back"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'A financing contingency lets the buyer exit if the loan isn''t approved, as the contract describes.', '["That''s the risk the contingency protects against.","The contingency excuses performance.","Nothing requires paying cash.",""]'::jsonb, 'Contingency: if this, then that.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'financing-contingency-cancel', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'A buyer makes an offer and dies before the seller accepts. The offer:', '["Converts to an option","Terminates","Becomes binding when the seller signs","Passes to the buyer''s estate to accept"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'An offer ends on the death or incapacity of either party before acceptance.', '["Nothing converts it.","","There''s no offer left to accept.","Offers don''t pass to estates."]'::jsonb, 'An offer dies with its maker.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'death-offeror-terminates-offer', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'You receive a lowball offer an hour after presenting a strong one, and the seller hasn''t responded yet. What should the agent do?', '["Reject it because it''s too low","Hold it until the strong offer is resolved","Tell the buyer''s agent it''s pointless","Present the new offer to the seller promptly"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Agents present all offers to the seller promptly. The seller decides.', '["Only the seller can reject an offer.","Withholding offers takes the decision away from the seller.","Dismissing it on the seller''s behalf oversteps the agent''s role.",""]'::jsonb, 'Present every offer. The seller picks.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-present-all-offers', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'A seller signs the buyer''s offer but, before telling anyone, the buyer calls to withdraw. Most likely:', '["The offer was withdrawn before acceptance was communicated, so there''s no contract","A contract exists because the seller signed","The buyer forfeits the earnest money","The seller can sue for specific performance"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Acceptance must be communicated to the offeror. The buyer revoked first.', '["","Signing alone isn''t enough; acceptance must be communicated.","Without a contract, there''s nothing to forfeit.","No contract exists to enforce."]'::jsonb, 'Accepted but unsaid isn''t accepted.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'acceptance-communicated', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'A counteroffer is a new offer that the original offeror may accept or reject.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","That''s right: the roles flip with each counter."]'::jsonb, 'Each counter flips the roles.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'counteroffer-new-offer', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'After a seller counteroffers, the buyer can still accept the original offer the seller rejected.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. A counteroffer kills the original offer.', '["The counteroffer rejected the original offer. It''s gone unless someone makes it again.",""]'::jsonb, 'Change anything, and you''ve rejected everything.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'original-offer-revived', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A buyer is purchasing a $350,000 home with a 10% down payment and has already deposited $5,000 earnest money that will be credited. How much more cash does the buyer need for the down payment at closing, ignoring closing costs?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":30000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'The $5,000 deposit is credited toward the $35,000 down payment, leaving $30,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Earnest money is credited back to the buyer.', 'Additional cash = (price × down payment %) − earnest money', '["Down payment: $350,000 × 0.10 = $35,000.","Subtract earnest money: $35,000 − $5,000 = $30,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'down-payment-after-earnest', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Which contingency lets a buyer exit or renegotiate after reviewing the home''s condition?', '["Inspection contingency","Sale-of-home contingency","Title contingency","Financing contingency"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'An inspection (due diligence) contingency covers the property''s physical condition.', '["","That depends on selling the buyer''s current home.","That''s about the condition of title, not the house.","That''s about loan approval."]'::jsonb, 'Inspection: look before you''re locked in.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'inspection-contingency', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A seller sends identical counteroffers to two buyers at the same time. The biggest risk is:', '["Neither buyer can respond","The listing automatically ends","The earnest money doubles","Both buyers accept, creating two binding contracts"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Multiple simultaneous counteroffers can each be accepted, leaving the seller bound twice. They should be worded to prevent that.', '["Both can respond; that''s the problem.","The listing continues.","Earnest money isn''t affected.",""]'::jsonb, 'Counter two at once, risk selling twice.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'multiple-counteroffers-risk', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'order', 1, 'recall', 'Put these steps in the order they happen when a counteroffer is accepted.', '["Buyer signs and delivers an offer","Seller changes the price and signs a counteroffer","Buyer signs the counteroffer","Seller learns the counteroffer was accepted, and a contract exists"]'::jsonb, '[0,1,2,3]'::jsonb, 'An offer, a counter that rejects it, acceptance of the counter, and communication of that acceptance form the contract.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Offer, counter, accept, tell.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'offer-to-contract-sequence', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'Earnest money a broker receives must be handled as trust funds, not mixed with the broker''s own money.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. Earnest money belongs to the transaction, not the broker.', '["","Mixing client money with the broker''s own is commingling, which is prohibited."]'::jsonb, 'Their money, separate account.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'earnest-money-trust', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.5-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.5', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'To create a contract, an acceptance must be:', '["Notarized","Accompanied by title insurance","Unconditional and match the offer''s terms","Recorded"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'Acceptance must agree to every term without conditions; otherwise it''s a counteroffer.', '["Notarization isn''t required for acceptance.","Title insurance isn''t part of acceptance.","","Recording isn''t required for a contract to form."]'::jsonb, 'Mirror the offer exactly.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'acceptance-must-be-unconditional', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-01', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'In an option to purchase, which party is obligated to complete the sale if the option is exercised?', '["The optionee","The optionor (owner)","Neither","Both, from the day it''s signed"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'The optionor must sell on the agreed terms if the optionee exercises; the optionee is free to walk away.', '["The optionee may choose not to buy.","","The owner is bound.","Only the owner is bound before exercise."]'::jsonb, 'The optionee has the option. The optionor is bound.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'optionee-not-obligated', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-02', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'For an option to be enforceable, the optionee must generally:', '["Record the option","Give consideration for the option","Have a loan approval","Close within 30 days"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'An option is a contract, so the optionee must give consideration, such as an option fee.', '["Recording gives notice but isn''t required between the parties.","","Financing isn''t required to hold an option.","Option periods vary by agreement."]'::jsonb, 'Pay for the right to decide.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'option-requires-consideration', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-03', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'An option is what kind of contract until it''s exercised?', '["Executed","Void","Bilateral","Unilateral"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Only the optionor makes a promise, so an option is unilateral until exercised.', '["Nothing has been performed yet.","A properly made option is valid.","Only the owner promises; the optionee doesn''t promise to buy.",""]'::jsonb, 'Uni means one promises.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'option-unilateral', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-04', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A right of first refusal gives the holder the right to:', '["Match a third party''s offer before the owner accepts it","Receive a commission","Buy at a fixed price whenever they want","Force the owner to sell"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'The holder gets the first chance to match a real offer.', '["","It''s a purchase right, not a commission.","That describes an option.","The owner can choose not to sell at all."]'::jsonb, 'First refusal: match it or lose it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'rofr-match', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-05', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'Under a land contract, who holds legal title until the price is paid in full?', '["The seller (vendor)","The county","The buyer (vendee)","A trustee"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'The vendor keeps legal title until the last installment is paid.', '["","The county doesn''t hold title.","The buyer holds equitable title and possession.","That describes a deed of trust, not a land contract."]'::jsonb, 'Pay it all, then the deed falls.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'land-contract-legal-title', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-06', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A developer holds an option on a lot and wants to sell the option to another builder. Generally the option:', '["Can be assigned unless the option agreement prohibits it","Can never be assigned","Can be assigned only after it''s exercised","Expires if assigned"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'Options are generally assignable unless the agreement says otherwise.', '["","Options are generally assignable.","Assignment can happen before exercise.","Assignment doesn''t end it."]'::jsonb, 'Assignable unless it says no.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'option-assignable', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-07', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'application', 'A tenant signs a lease that also gives them the right to buy the home at a set price within two years. This is a:', '["Lease with an option to purchase","Land contract","Right of first refusal","Novation"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'A lease combined with an option gives the tenant the right, not the duty, to buy.', '["","A land contract is a sale with installment payments.","A right of first refusal has no set price.","Novation replaces a contract."]'::jsonb, 'Lease now, option to own.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'lease-option', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-08', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'scenario', 2, 'application', 'You list a home whose tenant has a right of first refusal in the lease. You receive an acceptable offer. What should the agent do?', '["Accept the offer and tell the tenant later","Ignore the lease because the listing came later","Make sure the seller notifies the tenant of the offer terms as the lease requires before accepting it","Tell the buyer the tenant''s right is void"]'::jsonb, '2'::jsonb, 'The tenant must get the chance to match before the seller accepts.', '["Accepting first could breach the tenant''s right.","A recorded or known right of first refusal binds the owner.","","The agent can''t declare a contract right void."]'::jsonb, 'First refusal: match it or lose it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'agent-rofr-notify', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-09', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'An optionee who decides not to buy loses the option fee but owes nothing more.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True. The fee paid for the right, not for the property.', '["","Letting an option expire is the optionee''s right. They lose only what they paid for it."]'::jsonb, 'Pay for the right to decide.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'optionee-can-walk', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-10', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 2, 'recall', 'A right of first refusal usually sets the price the holder will pay.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'False. The holder matches whatever offer comes in.', '["A right of first refusal follows the price in a third party''s offer. A fixed price is a feature of an option.",""]'::jsonb, 'First refusal: match it or lose it.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'rofr-sets-price', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-11', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'tf', 1, 'recall', 'In a land contract, the buyer usually takes possession before receiving the deed.', '["True","False"]'::jsonb, '0'::jsonb, 'True.', '["","The buyer moves in and pays installments; the deed comes later."]'::jsonb, 'Live there now, deed later.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'land-contract-possession', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-12', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A buyer pays a $6,000 option fee, which the contract credits toward the $240,000 purchase price. The buyer exercises the option. How much of the price remains to be paid?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":234000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, 'The credited option fee reduces the remaining price to $234,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Credited fees come off the top.', 'Remaining = price − option fee credit', '["$240,000 − $6,000 = $234,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'option-fee-credit', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-13', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'number', 2, 'calculation', 'A buyer purchases land for $90,000 on a land contract with $10,000 down. Ignoring interest, after 48 monthly principal payments of $500, what principal balance remains?', '[]'::jsonb, '{"value":56000,"tolerance":0,"unit":"dollars"}'::jsonb, '$80,000 financed minus $24,000 paid leaves $56,000.', '[]'::jsonb, 'Pay it all, then the deed falls.', 'Balance = price − down payment − (payments × principal per payment)', '["Starting balance: $90,000 − $10,000 = $80,000.","Principal paid: 48 × $500 = $24,000.","Remaining: $80,000 − $24,000 = $56,000."]'::jsonb, null, 'land-contract-balance', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-14', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 2, 'recall', 'If the optionee doesn''t exercise an option before the deadline, the option:', '["Extends automatically","Expires, and the optionor keeps the option fee","Converts to a purchase contract","Becomes a right of first refusal"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'An unexercised option simply ends; the fee usually stays with the owner.', '["Extensions must be agreed.","","Nobody is obligated to buy.","It doesn''t convert into another right."]'::jsonb, 'Miss the window, lose the option.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'option-expires', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-15', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 3, 'application', 'Which is a significant risk for a buyer under a land contract?', '["The buyer can''t live in the home","The buyer can never get title","The buyer must pay a broker twice","The seller still holds legal title and could encumber it or fail to deliver a clear deed"]'::jsonb, '3'::jsonb, 'Because the vendor keeps legal title, liens or the vendor''s problems can cloud title. Buyers often record the contract and get title review.', '["Buyers usually take possession.","The buyer gets title after paying in full.","There''s no double commission.",""]'::jsonb, 'Seller keeps the deed, buyer keeps the risk.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'land-contract-risk-buyer', 'unverified'),
  ('N7.6-16', 'lesson', null, false, 'national', 'N7', 'N7.6', 'Content Outlines 01/15/2025 (#092901) [verify]', 'CON', 'mcq', 1, 'recall', 'A land contract is also called a:', '["Deed of trust","Contract for deed or installment sales contract","Lease option","Quitclaim"]'::jsonb, '1'::jsonb, 'Land contract, contract for deed, and installment sales contract describe the same arrangement.', '["A deed of trust secures a loan with a trustee holding title.","","A lease option is a lease with a right to buy.","A quitclaim is a deed."]'::jsonb, 'Contract for deed: the deed comes at the end.', null, '[]'::jsonb, null, 'land-contract-other-names', 'unverified')
